# Operator-owned deployment overlay (hosts, image pins, endpoints). Ship
# values-cluster.example.yaml instead; see docs/INSTALL.md.
k8s/helm/thingsflow/values-cluster.yaml
# Site-specific ingress (private hostnames / tailnet); the LB service next to it is
# a genericized reference example and stays tracked.
k8s/helm/thingsflow/extra-manifests/thingsflow-tailscale-ingress.yaml

# AI coding-agent artifacts — instructions, plans and session state are local tooling,
# not part of the published project.
.cursor/
.codex/
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Compiled Go test binaries (go test -c)
flow-core/bridge_test
*.test
flow-core/flow-core
site/

# Per-run outputs of the load generator. The calibrations (calibrate-*,
# verify-*, tb-smoke-*) ARE versioned: they are the client's baseline. What is
# worth nothing are the dumps of every level and their warm-ups, which on top of
# that carry timestamps and grow without bound. Two slipped in by accident.
benchmarks/scripts/loadgen2/results/run-*

# Of the fair ramp what gets published is the EVIDENCE (verdicts + per-level
# report) and not the working files: gate snapshots, intermediate lags and the
# raw log, which on top of that may carry operational details of the cluster.
benchmarks/results-fair*/.thr-*
benchmarks/results-fair*/.lag-*
benchmarks/results-fair*/ramp.log
benchmarks/results-fair*/ramp.pid

# ThingsBoard measurements: INTERNAL calibration, not publishable material.
#
# Publishing performance figures for another company's product, measured by us,
# on our infrastructure and with a backend chosen by us (DATABASE_TS_TYPE=sql
# instead of Cassandra/Timescale), is not defensible no matter how clean the
# methodology is. A table already had to be withdrawn because it stated a
# performance figure of theirs when that figure was their resource cage.
#
# We keep measuring them to know where we stand. They are not published.
benchmarks/results-fair*/thingsboard-*
benchmarks/helm/thingsboard-*/
benchmarks/profiles/fair-thingsboard.yaml
benchmarks/results-fair*/verdicts-internal.tsv

# AI agent files and sibling projects: they must NOT reach the public repo.
#
# They lived only in .git/info/exclude, which is LOCAL and does not travel with
# the clone: anyone who cloned the repo could add them with nothing stopping
# them. Here they do travel.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.claude/
.agents/
.cursor/
docs/superpowers/
gate-edge-energy/

# Local Python packaging artifacts (pip install -e / python -m build)
*.egg-info/
sdk/python/dist/

# Legion workflow state
.legion/
.legion/var/
